    "body": "Build the FF9 editor beyond the scaffold and the first Memoria CSV surfaces.\\n\\nCurrent proved baseline:\\n- A clean Steam install can populate verified vanilla Memoria CSV data without requiring the user to install Hades Workshop or Memoria first.\\n- Items, item effects, weapons, armor, support abilities, battle actions, character base stats, shops, and synthesis load through typed Table + Detail views and save to a mod-project overlay.\\n\\nRemaining work:\\n- Integrate the rest of Memoria's editable data surface.\\n- Resolve and implement enemies and encounters from the vanilla p0data containers or another source-proven export path.\\n- Add explicit coverage and rendered checks for each completed tab.\\n- Prove saved changes through the FF9 runtime before calling the editor complete.\\n\\nAcceptance boundary: no destination may look implemented while showing a placeholder or unavailable message. The issue remains actionable until the listed data and runtime boundaries are complete.",
